WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:02.568
 Well, Brandon,
man, congratulations.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.136
You just came off a
huge win against two

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:06.706
formidable opponents,
which means you're still

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.441
in contention for the
title of "Forged in Fire"

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:11.678
champion and that
check for $10,000.

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.780
But in order to
take home the win,

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:15.981
you've got a lot of
work ahead of you

00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:17.249
because you're
going to have to go

00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:19.452
against an undefeated
opponent who

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.654
has a lot of experience
in this forge,

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.790
and that guy is Ben Abbott.

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:25.992
BRANDON FRANKLIN: I've been
preparing for this competition,

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.327 line:8%
but Brendan seems to be
a very talented smith.

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:29.996
 You guys will have
eight hours to build

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:32.098
a blade from start to finish.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:33.332
 Brandon, you had
the opportunity

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:35.535
to choose what blade
and what technique

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:36.936
you're both going to use.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.404
So you've got a little
bit of an upper hand here.

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:40.573
But Ben, you ready to find
out what you're building?

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.175
 Yeah, let's do it.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.443
 The weapon that Brandon chose
from the "Forged in Fire" vault

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:48.815
is the messer.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.287
DOUG (VOICEOVER): The
messer traces its origins

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:56.122
back to 15th century Germany.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.790
While these swords
range in size,

00:00:57.856 --> 00:01:00.927
they are distinguished by the
intricate hilts and guards.

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:02.595
Back in season six
of "Forged in Fire,"

00:01:02.661 --> 00:01:04.998
two smiths were tasked to
recreate a massive version

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:07.132
of this weapon, where the
competition ultimately

00:01:07.232 --> 00:01:10.303
went to the lighter,
better balanced blade.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.805
 Smiths, you have eight hours
to complete your messer swords,

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:14.474
and that time starts now.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.408
 Going up against
Ben, being 4 and 0,

00:01:16.508 --> 00:01:18.978
I really hope that I'm
the one to beat him.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:20.613
I've got my tip roughly
where I want it.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:24.116 line:8%
And then I go over and create
this subtle distal taper.

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.085 line:8%
A lot of bladesmiths
grind to it,

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.788 line:8%
but I definitely want to
set myself up for less

00:01:28.854 --> 00:01:31.924
work later on at the grinder.

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:34.126
When I'm doing some
thermal cycling,

00:01:34.226 --> 00:01:35.561
I want to work on that guard.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:38.664
Do a quick test fit, and
it fits up the first time.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:41.233
And it's just this
huge sense of relief.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.637
HOST: Brandon's getting
ready for his quench.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.305
BRANDON FRANKLIN: We're
at a point of no return.

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:52.044
If I break this blade, I
could not finish this blade.

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:53.279
I see a nice straight blade.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:56.649
And then its end of
the tempering oven.

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:59.519
I'm really nervous about fitting
this handle up because I know

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.654
with the multiple
components going on,

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:04.890
it's going to eat
up a lot of my time.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.092
I'm kind of struggling
with the pin,

00:02:06.158 --> 00:02:07.459
so I've got to be careful here.

00:02:07.559 --> 00:02:09.795
I could risk cracking
my handle material.

00:02:09.895 --> 00:02:12.331
Luckily hitting it with a
hammer was enough to drive it

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:13.599
home where it needed to be.

00:02:13.699 --> 00:02:15.434
But I still have to
sharpen this thing too.

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.803
So now I really need
to move it up a gear

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:19.672
and get this thing done.

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:20.974
Time is ticking away.

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:23.276
And if I turn in a dull
blade, I'm going home.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:25.544
 I'm really putting all my eggs
in the basket of this damascus

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:27.045
because it's going
to take a long time.

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:28.247
But I think at the
end of the day,

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.916
the pattern is going
to be gorgeous,

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.617
and I'm going to end
up with a keen edge

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:34.420
that will hopefully not get
damaged in the strength test.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.855
There's a madness to my method.

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:38.857
 I've never seen a bigger
billet getting weld set

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:41.861
on this "Forged" floor.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:44.531
 Holy cow.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.731
I start to panic.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:49.068
It's so tall, I can't get
the compression that I

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.603
need all the way through.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.805
Instead of going to
blue at this point,

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:54.040
I have to go to the press.

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:55.574
It feels like my
billet is together now.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.444
Yeah, it's good.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:01.181
I finally started
working on a blade.

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:06.352
 That's the first
one in the oil.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:09.422
And I can see the terror
in Brandon's eyes.

00:03:11.924 --> 00:03:12.725
 It looks straight.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.327
I'm happy.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:17.897
I'm going for a relatively fine
edge on this because 80 CRV 2

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:19.866
can hold its shape pretty well.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:25.471
I've never made a
guard like this before.

00:03:25.537 --> 00:03:28.674
You make the guard
all in one piece.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:31.911
And then you have this side
guard that has a tang to it,

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:34.347
and you pin it over
on the far side.

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:35.982
One of the things
I know as a judge

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.017
is that the handle
has to be comfortable.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.986
But there are spots
on this handle

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:43.890
I can't get to with the grinder
because the knuckle bow is

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:45.724
there or the side
guard is there.

00:03:45.824 --> 00:03:47.993
In all the times that I
competed on this competition,

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.029
this one's been
more difficult. I

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:52.198
think it's because I
invested so much time

00:03:52.264 --> 00:03:53.566
up front working on the blade.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:56.769
So, at this point, the only
thing I can think to do

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:59.338
is grab a hand file and
work with a hand file.

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.373
My heart is beating
out of my chest.

00:04:01.473 --> 00:04:04.310
I might not finish this thing.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:09.181
 5, 4, 3, 2, 1.

00:04:09.281 --> 00:04:11.217
 Bladesmiths, turn
off your machines.

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:12.484
Put down your tools.

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:15.355
This eight-hour
competition is over.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.526
All right guys, we
are finally here.

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:21.727
And there's a lot on the line.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.696
Ben, if you take
home the win, you're

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.330
continuing your winning
streak, and going

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:27.266
on with a record of 5 and 0.

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:28.801
Now Brandon, if you
take home the win,

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.569
you're leaving here with the
title of "Forged in Fire"

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:33.505
champion and a
check for $10,000.

00:04:33.572 --> 00:04:35.641
In order for us to find out
which one of your blades

00:04:35.707 --> 00:04:37.142
is going to come out
on top, we have to put

00:04:37.242 --> 00:04:38.578
them through a series of tests.

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:40.546
So I'm going to give you
to Doug for the first one.

00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:48.454
 Bladesmiths, this is
the dynamic kill test.

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:51.090
To find out how lethal
your weapons are,

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.325
we take your swords,
cut through the vines,

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:57.096
and deliver some lethal
blows on this pig carcass.

00:04:57.196 --> 00:05:01.233
It's time to have fun.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:05.905
[music playing]

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:22.688
All right, guys.

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:25.091
First up, the
handle construction,

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:26.992
it's a little bit
on the blocky side.

00:05:27.092 --> 00:05:28.127
But it's comfortable.

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:28.994
Why?

00:05:29.061 --> 00:05:30.596
Because it's light.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:34.533
Every cut, every one of them was
very deep on this pig carcass.

00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:39.339
Overall, this eight-hour
master sword, it will KEAL.

00:05:42.641 --> 00:05:45.811
 I'm pretty confident that my
sword is not going to break.

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:48.547
But something might chip,
something might roll.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.282
Anything is possible.

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:54.286
I'm, I'm just nervous.

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:58.958
[music playing]

00:06:21.947 --> 00:06:25.551
 So right off the bat, I
really appreciate the flare

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:27.686
on a heavier blade
like this because it

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:29.455
does allow me to control it.

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:31.324
The weight of this
cuts very deep.

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:34.226
It thrusts nicely and
delivers all the way out.

00:06:34.292 --> 00:06:37.797
A blade like this, it will KEAL.

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:45.537
 All right, gentlemen,
a little bit of history.

00:06:45.604 --> 00:06:48.073
In 1570, Joachim
Meyer's treatise

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.976
on the use of the dussack
was published, the training

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:52.578
manual for the messer.

00:06:52.645 --> 00:06:54.279
So we know that it
was used by peasant

00:06:54.379 --> 00:06:56.615
soldiers as well as nobility.

00:06:56.715 --> 00:06:59.818
So to that end, our
dynamic strength test.

00:06:59.885 --> 00:07:01.320
Gentlemen, I'll be
taking your messers

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:03.322
and attacking our
armored warrior here.

00:07:03.422 --> 00:07:04.557
After that, we'll
see what kind of edge

00:07:04.623 --> 00:07:07.225
you have left by
slicing that painting.

00:07:07.292 --> 00:07:08.661
You guys ready?
- Oh yeah.

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:09.227
 Oh yeah.

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:10.096
DAVE BAKER: OK.

00:07:12.799 --> 00:07:17.203
[music playing]

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:33.252
All right.

00:07:33.319 --> 00:07:35.955
So right off, it's
taken a couple of rolls

00:07:36.021 --> 00:07:38.490
that I can feel with
the fingernail, and then

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:40.492
a couple of small minor chips.

00:07:40.592 --> 00:07:44.297
But for hitting armor,
that's not so bad.

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:46.732
All in all, our gold
anvil did a good job.

00:07:49.502 --> 00:07:54.073
[music playing]

00:08:16.328 --> 00:08:17.596
All right.

00:08:17.663 --> 00:08:20.432
So as far as the edge
goes, nothing's come off

00:08:20.499 --> 00:08:22.602
and nothing's
really rolled over.

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:25.905
So all in all, I think the red
anvil did a really nice job.

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:33.311
 Now guys, the
judges had a very

00:08:33.378 --> 00:08:34.647
difficult decision to make.

00:08:34.713 --> 00:08:36.548
And they came up
with a final decision

00:08:36.615 --> 00:08:38.016
that they both agreed upon.

00:08:38.116 --> 00:08:40.552
The winner of this "Forged
in Fire" competition

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:47.793
is Ben Abbott with
the red anvil.

00:08:47.894 --> 00:08:48.927
Congratulations.

00:08:49.027 --> 00:08:50.463
 No way.

00:08:50.563 --> 00:08:53.732
 Now Brandon, you absolutely
smoked this competition.

00:08:53.799 --> 00:08:56.302
But unfortunately, your messer
didn't make the cut today,

00:08:56.402 --> 00:08:58.637
and Dave Baker is
going to tell you why.

00:08:58.737 --> 00:09:01.173
 Brandon, you did a
great job on that messer.

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:03.008
It's fast and it's deadly.

00:09:03.108 --> 00:09:07.112
This basically came down to
damage and some design choices.

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:08.647
 Fair enough.

00:09:08.747 --> 00:09:10.416
 I can honestly say you're
one of the most talented smiths

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:12.050
I've ever laid my eyes on.

00:09:12.117 --> 00:09:13.352
 Thank you.

00:09:13.452 --> 00:09:15.087
 We appreciate all of your
hard work in this competition.

00:09:15.187 --> 00:09:16.588
But unfortunately, I'm going
to have to ask you to please

00:09:16.655 --> 00:09:17.790
step off the forge floor.

00:09:17.856 --> 00:09:19.090
 Thank you for the time, guys.

00:09:19.157 --> 00:09:19.825
 Thank you.

00:09:19.926 --> 00:09:20.492
Good job, man.

00:09:20.593 --> 00:09:21.260
 Awesome work.

00:09:21.327 --> 00:09:23.162
 Thanks, man.

00:09:23.262 --> 00:09:24.564 line:14%
Today just wasn't my day.

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:26.798 line:8%
But I think I turned in an
absolute phenomenal blade

00:09:26.865 --> 00:09:29.769
that stacked up against one
of the best, Ben Abbott.

00:09:32.338 --> 00:09:33.104
 All right, Ben.

00:09:33.171 --> 00:09:34.240
You did it.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.140
Your messer took
home the win again.

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:36.107
You're now 5 and 0, man.

00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:38.610
Congratulations.

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:40.612
 This was an extremely
close competition.

00:09:40.713 --> 00:09:42.514
Brandon is a hell
of a competitor.

00:09:42.581 --> 00:09:44.116
He made a really
good messer sword.

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:49.288
And I was actually practicing my
happy faced concession speech.

00:09:49.388 --> 00:09:51.022
 You ready for more?

00:09:51.089 --> 00:09:52.123
 Yep.

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:53.359
Let's do it.

00:09:53.459 --> 00:09:54.926
Any bladesmiths that
want to come in here

00:09:54.993 --> 00:09:58.793
and challenge me in my own
house, I'm here, ready for you.

